<%#
  ONE SHELF (2026-10-20): a folder inside every project, Projects/<project>/<name>/. Its name, the
  extensions that file into it as chips, one add form for the card, and the shelf's own settings --
  how its panel opens on a project page and which group it sits in. This was the Filing page's
  folder card (stage 4, S4-2; story 4.3) and keeps every class it had.

  A CHIP CARRIES ITS EXTENSION AND REMOVE, AND NOTHING ELSE. Moving `.dxf` from design to laser is
  Remove on one card and Add on the other -- two clicks on a rare action, where a folder picker per
  chip would put a select on all 124 of them, and a free-text folder field per chip is what made
  "dsign" a real, silent outcome on the flat page this replaced. Creating a NEW shelf is the name
  field at the foot of the page.

  NO RENAME AND NO REMOVE ON `other`: a name is a folder on disk in every project, and `other` is
  where an extension with no shelf files (Settings::ShelvesController#destroy refuses it too).

  Locals: shelf (a Maker::Shelf), by_folder (folder name to its rules, grouped once in #index --
  a `where` here would be a query per card), groups (the user's groups, for the Group menu).
%>
<section class="filing-card shelf-card">
  <div class="shelf-card-head">
    <h2 class="filing-folder mono"><%= shelf.name %>/</h2>
    <% unless shelf.fallback? %>
      <%= button_to "Remove shelf", settings_shelf_path(shelf), method: :delete,
                    class: "linkbtn danger small",
                    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove the #{shelf.name}/ shelf? " \
                                                    "Its extensions will file into other." } } %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% rules = by_folder[shelf.name] || [] %>
  <ul class="filing-exts">
    <% rules.each do |rule| %>
      <li class="chip filing-chip">
        <span class="mono">.<%= rule.ext %></span>
        <%= button_to "Remove", settings_filing_rule_path(rule), method: :delete,
                      class: "linkbtn danger small",
                      form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Remove the filing rule for .#{rule.ext}? " \
                                                      "It will file into other until you add a new one." } } %>
      </li>
    <% end %>
    <% if rules.empty? %>
      <li class="empty inline">Nothing files here yet.</li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
  <%# scope: :filing_rule names the params at all (this form has no model object), which is what
      Settings::FilingRulesController#create requires -- CLAUDE.md's form-scope rule, asserted on
      the RENDERED field names in settings_shelves_test.rb. The folder rides as a hidden field so
      adding an extension to this card is one text box.

      id: nil ON EVERY FIELD IN THIS CARD. There is one of each form per CARD, and form_with derives
      an id from the scope alone -- so the default spelling puts a dozen elements with id
      "filing_rule_ext" (or "shelf_default_view") on one page, which is invalid HTML and hands
      getElementById an arbitrary one of them. Each label WRAPS its control, so the association is
      implicit and survives having no id at all; the params are unaffected, which is why the
      rendered-field-name assertions still read the same. %>
  <%= form_with url: settings_filing_rules_path, scope: :filing_rule, class: "settings-add filing-add" do |f| %>
    <%= f.hidden_field :folder, value: shelf.name, id: nil %>
    <label>
      <span>Add extension</span>
      <%= f.text_field :ext, required: true, placeholder: "lbrn", id: nil %>
    </label>
    <%= f.submit "Add", class: "btn ghost small" %>
  <% end %>
  <%# scope: :shelf is what Settings::ShelvesController#update requires. A namespaced model scopes
      to maker_shelf on its own, which that action would refuse as a missing param (section 14d). %>
  <%= form_with model: shelf, url: settings_shelf_path(shelf), scope: :shelf, method: :patch,
                class: "shelf-settings" do |f| %>
    <label>
      <span>View</span>
      <%= f.select :default_view,
                   [ [ "Automatic", "" ], *Maker::Project::VIEWS.map { |v| [ v.capitalize, v ] } ],
                   {}, id: nil %>
    </label>
    <label>
      <span>Group</span>
      <%= f.select :shelf_group_id, [ [ "None", "" ], *groups.map { |g| [ g.name, g.id ] } ],
                   {}, id: nil %>
    </label>
    <%= f.submit "Save", class: "btn ghost small" %>
  <% end %>
</section>
